WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've had such
an eclectic career.

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.236 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Are there certain roles

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you get approached for
more than others?

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
I mean, people --

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, people know
"The Devil Wears Prada."

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which is, you know,
a great film.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.880 size:81% position:41%
Or "The Hunger Games"
or "The Lovely Bones,"

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is very disturbing,
you know.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, yeah, there's a lot.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Easy A," too, is one.
-Oh, that's nice.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
So, it's nice, yeah.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- It kind of
came out of nowhere.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.725
Sam Rockwell was hosting "SNL."
-Oh, my God, yeah.

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:29.963
-And Pete Davidson did a rap
about you called "Tucci Gang."

00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here's -- there's Sam as you.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With Pete Davidson.
And there -- there's Sam.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, uh, now obviously,

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.340
this must have been --
it was unexpected for me.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must have been completely
unexpected for you.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.412
-I was completely shocked.
My publicist called, said,

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:94% position:6%
"They need you to do an image
or say something

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
for, you know,
'Saturday Night Live.'"

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:51.084 line:92%
And I was like, "What is it?

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.519
I don't know what you're
talking about," you know.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- I knew what
"Saturday Night Live" was.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:56.322 line:92%
I mean, yeah, I did, yeah.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:58.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
But once you -- you know,
I stopped watching it

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
once you left.
-Thank you.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Um...uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:05.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Sam I've known
for a really long time.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:06.433 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, anyway, I said,
"Yeah, sure."

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.003
And they told me what they --
and then I saw what they did.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:11.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And of course, I didn't know

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:14.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
the genesis, I didn't know
what it was based on.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
So my children
had to explain to me

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:17.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
what it was and showed me
the video.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like, "Oh, wow,
that's good."

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it's brilliant,
and I was very flattered.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.450 line:92%
-And was this something that --

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can only imagine
how many people --

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, when somebody --
when you see something

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.089
that is about your friends,
so many people must have

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:31.157
texted you and reached out
and said, "Have you seen it?"

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah. No, they were
flipped out by it.

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah. I mean, I was, too.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I was
completely shocked.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is wonderful
that your children

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
had to explain it to you.
I think that's --

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I know, I know, yeah.
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:43.303 size:84% position:42%
-I'm looking forward
to that part of my life

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:46.172
where I can stop trying to have
any connection to pop culture,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they can just --
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:48.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just tell you everything.
-Yeah. Oh.

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:50.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you go, "Well,
how do you get it --"

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, just give it to me."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.749 size:84% position:42%
-You're a cook as well.
-Yeah, I like to cook.

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:59.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do your children like
your cooking?

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, they do, yes.
-That's great.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the two who are at
university now are quite sad,

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they don't have
the cooking.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So, when they come home,

00:02:06.493 --> 00:02:09.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
I make sure to make as much
stuff as possible.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:10.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just make sauces
or something

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
to give them
so they can take it home.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's very kind.
That's very kind and helpful.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you've had
a couple of cookbooks.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:18.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have. I put one
together a long time ago

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.140 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that my parents did with

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
an Italian chef,
Gianni Scappin.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.811
And then my wife and I did one
a few years ago together, yeah.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was that a fun process,
building together the recipes

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
for a cookbook?
-It is. It's fun.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.886
But it is such hard work.
It's incredibly hard work

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sort of
piece them all together.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you have to have
a hundred recipes.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:37.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Really,

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.525 size:88% position:44% line:92%
to have a real cookbook.

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the testing of them
will take you a year.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-At least a year.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.697 size:78% position:39%
-And how is your wife
as a collaborator?

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:47.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, she's amazing.
Well, she's a literary agent.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wonderful.
-But, so, she's incredible.

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.638 line:92%
And she's a great cook, too.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what is the cookbook
that you did with her called?

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:56.576 line:92%
-It's called "The Tucci Table."

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's very good.
-Yes. Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.581
She said, "Well, we could
call it 'Tucci and Friend'

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
or something."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
She goes, "Because you have
one friend.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:06.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's face it," you know.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:12.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- but it's basically
what we would cook

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
throughout a year.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:14.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For your friends
and your family.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:15.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
"Table for Tucci"?

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Table for Tucci."
-You could do that next time.

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.665
-There you go, yeah.
-Now you gotta do a third book.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you. Thank you. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:21.701
-Thanks so much for being here.
-Thank you.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really a pleasure
to speak to you.

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.704 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thanks a lot.

